    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "2a. Markers — choose what the harness reads (declare, don't slurp)",
      "prov:value": "Owner, 2026-10-30T12:41Z: *\"a harness can point to a repo, but doesnt want to\nautomatically slurpo up all content in a repo. harness desclares what it it\npays attention to in the repo.\"* The principle is\n[directory-conventions](../../kg/kg-core/directory-conventions.md) §\"A marker\ndeclares what is read, and nothing else is\".",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-30T12:41Z",
        "owner"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. The conversion itself",
      "prov:value": "**If the remote is empty, push `main` first.** A repository with work\nlocally can still have an empty remote, and GitHub makes the first branch\npushed to an empty repository its default. Run `init-folio` or push `main`\nbefore any feature branch (litlfred/dth-hrh, owner 2026-10-14).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-14",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "4. The conversion itself",
      "prov:value": "**If `main` has no harness yet, land a setup-only PR first.** A fork or an\nexisting repository whose `main` has no `index.config.json` and\n`index.lock.json` gives the full PR checks nothing to compare against: the\nbase side fails before any test runs, and the PR's own gates are skipped\n(https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/1139). So open one small PR with only what `folio_init`\nwrites and the pins, merge it, and only then branch for content. Draft-tier\nchecks never build the base, so this does not show until the content PR\nleaves draft (litlfred/dth-sc#1, owner 2026-10-31).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "litlfred/dth-sc#1",
        "https://github.com/litlfred/cat-harness-tools/issues/1139",
        "2026-10-31",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "5. Publishing — provision `gh-pages` first; an overlay needs it too",
      "prov:value": "An overlay never reaches [`getting-started`](getting-started.md) §5 by\nitself, so this section repeats the one step a publishing route cannot skip:\n**provision `gh-pages` before GitHub Pages is switched on.** Owner,\n2026-10-01: *\"need to create gh-pages branch before can turn on\"*; repeated\n2026-10-07: *\"need to create gh-pages before can deploy\"* (issue #2417).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#2417",
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01",
        "2026-10-07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/conduct/conduct-core/repo-conversion.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Worked example — litlfred/test",
      "prov:value": "### Worked example — litlfred/test\n\nlitlfred/test is an overlay that remote-mounts its harness layers\n(its lock is the legacy `test.mount-lock.json` until it converts to `index.config.json` and `index.lock.json`: [`index-config`](../../kg/kg-core/index-config.md)) and publishes its L1 site from `main` through a\nworkflow that pushes `gh-pages` (`.github/workflows/l1-kg.yml`). Its first\nplan, in litlfred/test#3, said \"Pages source: GitHub Actions\" and had no\nprovisioning step. The owner caught it. In\n[litlfred/test#5](https://github.com/litlfred/test/pull/5) the branch was\nprovisioned as `860f9c2` — an orphan commit holding exactly `index.html` and\n`.nojekyll`, which is what `--provision` writes.\n\nRun against that repository today, `pages-bootstrap.ts` reports `gh-pages\nbranch: present on origin` and `Pages source expected: Deploy from a branch:\ngh-pages, / (root)`. Run against a copy whose remote has no `gh-pages`, it\nstops at `UNPROVISIONED` and exits 3, naming `--provision` — the step the\noriginal plan skipped.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "litlfred/test#3",
        "litlfred/test#5",
        "https://github.com/litlfred/test/pull/5",
        "owner"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
